    "narrative": "Our primary engine for today is **Lawrence Butler**, who commands the highest score of 73.41. Batting out of the leadoff spot against Jared Jones, **Butler** benefits from a massive 13% dynamic platoon boost and a favorable 10% park factor adjustment, positioning him as an elite play despite the pitcher\u2019s respectable 3.94 xERA. Alongside him, **Bryson Stott** (62.55) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (61.72) provide the necessary stability in the infield. **Stott** is particularly attractive today; facing Gusto, he gains a 4% boost from park conditions and an additional 4% for the opposing pitcher's high stolen base allowance (88% success rate), which aligns perfectly with our organizational mandate to maximize speed. **Tyler Freeman** (60.46) also edges into the \"Strong\" tier, buoyed by an 8% bump from the #2 spot and favorable winds, even while facing the tough Shota Imanaga.\n\nThe decision to start **Gleyber Torres** at 48.29 was our most difficult call, as he nearly landed on the bench in favor of our reserve depth. While his 10% leadoff order boost keeps him in the mix, a 13% negative platoon adjustment against Teng suppresses his ceiling, making him a marginal play. We are monitoring the status of **Jonathan Aranda** and **Geraldo Perdomo** closely; as their lineups are currently pending, a shift in batting order could further dampen their projections. We remain frustrated by the high-value production currently sidelined on the IL, specifically **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, **Will Smith**, and **Daulton Varsho**. Their absence forces us to lean on high-risk, high-upside options like **Ryan Waldschmidt** (53.64), who despite a weak 9th-order placement, retains value due to a favorable matchup against Walbert Ure\u00f1a. We are avoiding any unnecessary risk with depth players like **Taylor Ward**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Matt Chapman**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, or **Drew Gilbert**, keeping them on the bench to preserve our limited game caps for more optimal splits.",
